                <note rend="inline" type="source">637.0023/93a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Howell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-29T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>96. Mr. Lawrence A. Crosby, of the firm of Sullivan and Cromwell, is arriving at
                    Habana Wednesday morning aboard the steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Toloa</hi>, and desires to present the views of certain American interests to
                    President Zayas Wednesday afternoon.</p>
                <p>From the text of the Tarafa Bill passed by both Houses of the Cuban Congress,
                    given to the Department by Messrs. Sullivan and Cromwell, it appears that the
                    rights of American interests are very seriously affected by the provisions of
                    the Bill, and the Department, therefore, desires that those interested should be
                    afforded a hearing by President Zayas prior to his taking any definite action on
                    the Bill. You will, therefore, request an interview with President Zayas for
                    Wednesday afternoon for Mr. Crosby to present to the President’s consideration
                    information regarding the manner in which American interests are prejudiced. The
                    Department desires that you should accompany Mr. Crosby and state that the
                    Department would be glad if the President would carefully consider the points
                    brought out by Mr. Crosby.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
